{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-q2-fmt-sort/ntail-bracket-sharp-s-accdb",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-SORT-3",
    "SORT-CHECK",
    "Length510 boundary",
    "Compound framing"
  ],
  "description": "Branch R-SORT-3 Length510 boundary, locating the length where a trailing key field stops deciding order (public side), one character kind per probe (this one: U+00DF), on an ACCDB. LA(ID, K Text(255), N Long) with non-unique IX_KN on (K, N) built before the rows; for each length 248 to 255 two rows with K = the character repeated to that length, N = 2 inserted first (ID 10k+1) and N = 1 second (ID 10k+2), k = 1 to 8. Reads the IX_KN walk (a pair listed with the N = 1 row first keeps N in the key; the N = 2 row first means the tie fell to insertion order), the backward walk, and SQL ORDER BY K, N. The first card found the loss at 253 and 255 but not 254 for the acute e, so every length from 248 to 255 is asked separately. Asks the first length at which N stops deciding order, whether it is monotonic in length, and whether the answer depends on the index (SQL order is read on the same table).",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
